9022 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_1000398 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002220 obo:UBERON_0006841)))\n\n  Line 32858: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:24928499\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:27889329\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033054 \"A cell that is adjacent to a vessel. A perivascular cell plays a crucial role in maintaining vascular function and tissue homeostasis. This cell type regulates vessel integrity and flow dynamics.\")\n\n  Line 32862: EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4033054 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000000 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002220 obo:UBERON_0002049)))\n\n  Line 33861: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21252048\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:36032088\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4047023 \"A fibroblast located in the lamina propria of the intestinal mucosa. This cell expresses PDGFRα and CD81 and is negative for α-smooth muscle actin (α-SMA). This cell is predominantly located in the small intestine adjacent to myofibroblasts surrounding the crypts. It is capable of synthesizing extracellular matrix components and structural proteins such as collagen and elastin.\")\n\n  Line 34159: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30270042\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33430285\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33916891\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37080817\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4052007 \"A fibroblast located adjacent to the intestinal epithelium in both the small intestine and colon, specifically around the crypts. This cell is characterized by the expression of  PDGFRα and various collagen isoforms, including COL4A5 and COL4A6. It secretes signalling molecules like TGF-β, Wnt ligands, and BMPs, which are crucial for epithelial homeostasis, intestinal stem cell support, and basement membrane formation.\")\n\n  Line 34167: SubClassOf(obo:CL_4052007 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002220 obo:UBERON_0001277))\n\n  Line 34171: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33916891\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:/10.1371/journal.pbio.3001032\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4052008 \"A subepithelial intestinal fibroblast that is located adjacent to the base of the crypt of Lieberkühn, near the intestinal stem cells. Characterized by low PDGFRα expression, this cell is crucial for maintaining the intestinal stem cell niche. Crypt-bottom fibroblast secretes key signaling molecules including canonical Wnt ligands (Wnt2, Wnt2b), Wnt potentiators (Rspo3), and BMP inhibitors (Grem1), which collectively regulate intestinal stem cell function and epithelial homeostasis.\")\n\n  Line 34178: SubClassOf(obo:CL_4052008 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002220 obo:CL_0002250))\n\n  Line 34179: SubClassOf(obo:CL_4052008 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002220 obo:UBERON_0013739))\n\n  Line 34183: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33916891\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:/10.1371/journal.pbio.3001032\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4052009 \"A subepithelial intestinal fibroblast that is located adjacent to the top of the crypt of Lieberkuhn. Characterized by high experession of PDGFRα, this cell secretes a range of signaling factors, including WNTs and BMPs, that drive epithelial differentiation, creating a gradient that regulates the balance between stem cell maintenance and differentiation.\")\n\n  Line 34192: SubClassOf(obo:CL_4052009 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002220 obo:UBERON_0013740))\n\n  Line 35419: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:25356439\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32341164\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:39829808\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_7770002 \"A trabecular meshwork cell of the juxtacanalicular tissue (JCT), characterized by a spindle-shaped, fibroblast-like morphology within a loose extracellular matrix immediately adjacent to Schlemm's canal. It expresses CHI3L1 (human and mouse) and ANGPTL7 (human), as well as smooth muscle actin for contractility. Unlike other trabecular meshwork cells, it does not form monolayers but exists in a loose network, regulating aqueous humor outflow resistance through continuous ECM remodelling, mechanotransduction, and formation of intracellular pores historically called giant vacuoles.\")\n","metadata":{"matches":30,"truncated":false},"title":"RO_0002220|adjacent to","time":{"start":1778978843418,"end":1778978843463}},"id":"prt_e3366eb08001jUyjgdKVIowsB8","sessionID":"ses_1cc99a625ffei0cFSQ4yg684Kg","messageID":"msg_e3366b55e001ZSyT2GA153olif"}}
