{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778979062718,"sessionID":"ses_1cc99a625ffei0cFSQ4yg684Kg","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_yu6SYRSM4Ru5sV7nrvV1h4sC","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n+Addressed in PR #<NN>.\n+\n+Updated the five existing otic fibrocyte subclasses with revised spiral ligament fibrocyte labels, refreshed definitions and PMIDs, and added available location axioms.\n*** Add File: /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/PR_COMMENTS.md\n+Updated the five existing otic fibrocyte subclasses in `src/ontology/cl-edit.owl` to align with issue #3408.\n+\n+What changed:\n+- Relabeled the existing subclasses to the spiral ligament fibrocyte naming scheme:\n+  - `CL_0002670` -> `type I spiral ligament fibrocyte`\n+  - `CL_0002666` -> `type II spiral ligament fibrocyte`\n+  - `CL_0002669` -> `type III spiral ligament fibrocyte`\n+  - `CL_0002668` -> `type IV spiral ligament fibrocyte`\n+  - `CL_0002667` -> `type V spiral ligament fibrocyte`\n+- Kept the pre-existing Roman numeral otic names as exact synonyms and added the Arabic-number otic names as broad synonyms, per the issue request.\n+- Rewrote the definitions using the issue-provided text and added the requested PMIDs without removing the older references already on the terms.\n+- Reparented these subclasses from the broader `otic fibrocyte` term to `spiral ligament fibrocyte` (`CL_0020005`).\n+- Added available anatomical restrictions from the issue where I could ground them safely:\n+  - `part of some spiral ligament` for all five subclasses\n+  - `adjacent to some stria vascularis of cochlear duct` for type I and type V\n+  - `adjacent to some spiral prominence of cochlear duct` for type II\n+  - `adjacent to some otic capsule` for type III\n+- Added issue tracker annotations linking each edited term back to issue #3408.\n+- Added the requested exact synonym `tension fibroblast` to type III.\n+\n+Modeling notes:\n+- The imported issue title says `type I-IV`, but the body contains explicit requested updates for type V as well. I followed the detailed body and updated all five existing subclasses.\n+- I did not add an additional logical axiom for type IV beyond `part of some spiral ligament`, because the issue text did not provide a stable target anatomy ID I could verify locally for `crista basilaris`/`basilar crest`.\n+\n+Validation performed:\n+- Ran `robot convert -i src/ontology/cl-edit.owl -o /tmp/opencode/cl-edit.ofn` to confirm the edited ontology still parses.\n+\n+Completed checklist:\n+- [x] Read the imported issue context\n+- [x] Inspected the existing fibrocyte terms in `cl-edit.owl`\n+- [x] Updated labels, synonyms, definitions, and references\n+- [x] Added available anatomical axioms\n+- [x] Validated ontology syntax with ROBOT\n+- [x] Committed only the edited ontology file\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\nA PR_COMMENTS.md","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n===================================================================\n--- /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n+++ /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,3 @@\n+Addressed in PR #<NN>.\n+\n+Updated the five existing otic fibrocyte subclasses with revised spiral ligament fibrocyte labels, refreshed definitions and PMIDs, and added available location axioms.\n\nIndex: /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/PR_COMMENTS.md\n===================================================================\n--- /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/PR_COMMENTS.md\n+++ /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/PR_COMMENTS.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,34 @@\n+Updated the five existing otic fibrocyte subclasses in `src/ontology/cl-edit.owl` to align with issue #3408.\n+\n+What changed:\n+- Relabeled the existing subclasses to the spiral ligame